{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36551-converting-classic-world-of-darkness-to-a-new-system","id":36551,"title":"Converting Classic World of Darkness to a new system?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-24T14:12:58-08:00","id":36551,"title":"Converting Classic World of Darkness to a new system?","content":"Okay guys, I had an idea of converting the original five World of Darkness games plus the Mortals rules to the Tri-Stat system of Big Eyes Small Mouth 3rd Edition, and I am wondering what would be the best way to do this. I figured each Clan, Tribe, Tradition, Guild, and Kith would be a template or sub-template, but converting Disciplines, Gifts, and especially Spheres to BESM rules would be tricky.<br /> <br /> Essentially this fan product is a means to both test a rules conversion and do a remake of the Classic World of Darkness that is metaplot-free and light on the personal horror (Nothing wrong with personal horror, but it's not really my thing), and have a system to better reflect these changes.<br /> <br /> Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Mortals, and Changeling are definitely getting converted, and Wraith probably is as well. Reckoning, KOTE, and Demon are left in the dust, and other characters from other anime and anime genres are in the World of Darkness as well (Such as Magical Girls).<br /> <br /> Now, I figured I would start with Vampire, and then work my way through Werewolf and Mage. I do not own Wraith or Changeling, so I'd need help converting those games as well.<br /> <br /> I'm going to start with Vampire: The Masquerade, and there would be several templates (Age) and sub-templates (Clan). Here's the general outlines I have for the main templates...<br /> <br /> Fledgling (Equivalent to 13th Generation)<br /> Neonate (Equivalent to 11th Generation)<br /> Ancilla (Equivalent to 9th Generation)<br /> Elder (Equivalent to 7th Generation)<br /> Luminary (Equivalent to 6th Generation)<br /> Ancient (Equivalent to 5th Generation)<br /> Methuselah (Equivalent to 4th Generation)<br /> <br /> All thirteen clans are in play, and I may convert the bloodlines later.<br /> <br /> First, I need to make the details for the templates and then Disciplines applicable to the Clans.<br /> <br /> Is anybody willing to help me in the conversions of Vampire: The Masquerade to Big Eyes Small Mouth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T07:21:47-07:00","id":124471,"title":"","content":"It appears that the number of people who would find such a specific conversion useful is very small. If I were to convert to any system, it would be FATE, largely because it the only dice system that employs a probability curve that is actually found in nature (the Bell Curve).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T15:42:56-07:00","id":124819,"title":"","content":"Dropping by to second FATE. It's magnificent and free!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T16:24:44-07:00","id":124843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36551-converting-classic-world-of-darkness-to-a-new-system?p=124471#post124471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears that the number of people who would find such a specific conversion useful is very small. If I were to convert to any system, it would be FATE, largely because it the only dice system that employs a probability curve that is actually found in nature (the Bell Curve).</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, the OP is asking for help converting to BESM. I don't own BESM 3e, so I can't help much there. Telling them to go to other systems doesn't seem very helpful.<br /> <br /> Second, as a side note, FATE is not the only dice system that uses a normal distribution curve. GURPs for example, generates just as much of a normal curve as FATE does. The bell curve is also far from the only distribution curve found in nature. A simple and common example are F-distributions.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> Third, to the OP:<br /> <br /> I can't help much on the systems, but is there a particular reason why Magic Girls wouldn't just be a kind of mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T17:41:50-07:00","id":124878,"title":"","content":"I fear that I am only familiar with one of the older BESM editions, and not particularly familiar at that. However, I would offer the advice that you might want to start with just the Fledgling age template, and put the real focus on each Clan template; Once you know the clans are playable at low levels, you can more easily scale upwards for higher age templates.<br /> <br /> Also, you might consider making a second thread on RPG.net, where there are more forum-goers with experience in both World of Darkness _and_ BESM. Having both threads should help expand your reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T16:45:28-07:00","id":125397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36551-converting-classic-world-of-darkness-to-a-new-system?p=124843#post124843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bell curve is also far from the only distribution curve found in nature. A simple and common example are F-distributions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Binomial distributions (which is approximately what WoD systems are based on barring the special dice rules) occur a lot as well for that matter. People tend to see Normal distributions everywhere because of the Central Limit Theorem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redford_Blade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36551-converting-classic-world-of-darkness-to-a-new-system?p=124878#post124878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you might consider making a second thread on RPG.net, where there are more forum-goers with experience in both World of Darkness _and_ BESM. Having both threads should help expand your reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1. This is a very good idea. I don't know enough about BESM to be any help unfortunately. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T20:27:31-07:00","id":127211,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll dig out my copy of BESM3e when I get home. But be warned: there\u2019s a significant design philosophy mismatch between BESM (which is a point accounting system that attaches point costs to everything) and the cWoD games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T22:58:14-07:00","id":128767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36551-converting-classic-world-of-darkness-to-a-new-system?p=124843#post124843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Telling them to go to other systems doesn't seem very helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Telling someone to leave a thread opener that had received zero replies in months in that abandoned state is even less helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T23:28:21-07:00","id":128777,"title":"","content":"I don't particularly see how. I at least thought of something relevant to the OP's goals to say. If you want to bump/necro a thread because you want to see if giving it some attention might get it some replies this time around? Cool. I can respect that. There are also dozens of ways I can think of off the top of my head to accomplish that without posting something completely unhelpful to the OP's goal in the process.<br /> <br /> You'll notice I didn't say, &quot;necroing this thread is stupid,&quot; or, &quot;what's the point, this thread was dead?&quot; I called you out for what you suggested relevant to the goal of the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}